ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 24108, Sep. 21, 2012>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on January 18, 2013.
Article 2 (Special cases concerning the appointment of faculty and staff members)
(1) Public officials who are faculty members affiliated with the former Incheon University and who do not wish to be appointed as faculty members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under Article 5(5) of the Addenda to the Act shall belong to Incheon Metropolitan City while retaining their status as public officials, and their authorized personnel quota shall be deemed separately established.
(2) Faculty members under paragraph (1) shall be deemed dispatched to Incheon National University, a national university corporation under Article 30-4 of the Local Public Officials Act. In such cases, notwithstanding Article 27-2(2) of the Local Public Officials Appointment Decree, the dispatch period shall be 5 years.
(3) Faculty members under paragraph (1) shall be deemed faculty members of a public university in applying the Local Public Officials Remuneration Regulations, the Regulations on Allowances for Local Public Officials, and the Regulations on Payment of Honorary Retirement Allowances, etc. for Local Public Officials.
(4) Public officials personnel-related statutes and regulations shall apply mutatis mutandis to personnel management of faculty members dispatched under paragraph (2); provided, the Mayor of Incheon Metropolitan City may separately determine matters necessary for efficient personnel management.
(5) Staff members affiliated with the former Incheon University who do not wish to be appointed as staff members of Incheon National University, a national university corporation under Article 5(5) of the Addenda to the Act shall belong to Incheon Metropolitan City while retaining their status as public officials for 1 year after the establishment of Incheon National University, a national university corporation, and their authorized personnel quota shall be deemed separately established.
(6) Matters concerning guarantee of status, service relations, etc. of staff members under paragraph (5) that are not prescribed in this Decree shall be governed by the Local Public Officials Act.
Article 3 (Appropriation and payment of State contributions)
(1) The State shall appropriate in the budget each year State compensation funds and State support funds under Article 7(3) and (6) of the Addenda to the Act (hereinafter referred to as "State compensation funds, etc."). In such cases, where there is any deficiency from the previous year, such deficiency shall also be appropriated.
(2) By March 31 of each year, the Pension Corporation for Private School Teachers and Staff under the Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act shall calculate the estimated amount required for the following year for State compensation funds, etc., clarify details of such calculation, and submit them to the head of the relevant central administrative agency.
(3) The head of the relevant central administrative agency shall pay State compensation funds, etc. to the pension collection agency in 4 installments each year by no later than 1 month before the commencement of each quarter, and the pension collection agency receiving such payment shall issue a receipt to the head of the relevant central administrative agency and, without delay, send a notice of deposit to the Pension Corporation for Private School Teachers and Staff under the Private School Teachers and Staff Pension Act.
(4) Where the amount paid by the State as State compensation funds, etc. by the end of the relevant fiscal year is less or more than the actual expenses incurred, settlement thereof shall be made by January 31 of the following year, and where settlement is not made by January 31 of the following year (including cases where the full amount is not paid to the Corporation within the relevant fiscal year), settlement shall be made by adding interest to such amount as principal.
(5) Interest under paragraph (4) shall be calculated at the highest fixed deposit interest rate applied as of January 1 of the relevant year by a bank established under the Banking Act that conducts business nationwide, and shall be calculated on a compound interest basis for each fiscal year.

